  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) is the current best at 0.650 acc, outperforming config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.591. This confirms multiprofile+avgpool is the right structural choice and that encoder quality matters (~6% gain). Uncertainty: we have not yet tested whether scgpt, the third available encoder, surpasses scvi_n200 under identical conditions. Question tested: config_008 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) provides a clean A/B comparison of scgpt vs scvi_n200 while holding profile setting and aggregation constant, isolating the encoder/representation effect. Why best next step: Before investing limited budget in multimodal fusion experiments (where image-only performance is very weak at 0.21), we need to confirm which RNA encoder is optimal. If scgpt outperforms scvi_n200, it changes the foundation for all downstream multimodal configs; if it does not, we lock in scvi_n200 and can confidently move to multimodal testing. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most impactful remaining design choice within the RNA-only space."
}

